From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0087] anv: Xe2 HEVC encode VDENC_PIPE_MODE_SELECT reference prefetch and DW5 as media-driver

On top of 0084 (installed Mesa 935ef655 = src/mesa-onehandle + 0084 = src/mesa-videotu). Built from a file copy
(src/mesa-hevctu, build-hevctu; same meson options as build-vt, release, x86_64). NOT installed.

Xe2 only (Gen12/12.5 unchanged). ANV's HEVC encoder programmed VDENC_PIPE_MODE_SELECT DW2/DW3 with the genxml
defaults (top prefetch mode 1, numVerticalReqMinus1 11, source TLB prefetch on with offset 4: what media-driver
programs for Xe3, encode_hevc_basic_feature_xe3_lpm_base.cpp) and left DW5 bit 17 clear. media-driver's
Xe2_HPM HEVC VDEnc path:
- DW2: no HEVC override (HevcBasicFeature / HevcVdencPkt MHW_SETPAR(VDENC_PIPE_MODE_SELECT)), so the
  MHW_PAR_T(VDENC_PIPE_MODE_SELECT) defaults (mhw_vdbox_vdenc_cmdpar.h): HME region prefetch 1, top prefetch
  mode 0, left prefetch at wrap around 1, verticalShift32Minus1 2, hzShift32Minus1 3, numVerticalReqMinus1 6,
  numHzReqMinus1 2, prefetch offset 0. ANV's Xe2 AV1 encoder already uses exactly these.
- DW3: VDENC_PIPE_MODE_SELECT_CMD constructor zeros (mhw_vdbox_vdenc_hwcmd_xe2_hpm.h), not set by HEVC.
- DW5 bit 17 = VdencPipeModeSelectPar0 = 1 (encode_hevc_vdenc_packet.cpp, unless WaEnableOnlyASteppingFeatures).
  No DW5 bit 8 for HEVC (AVC only).
Prefetch fields only change memory access timing; DW5 bit 17 is undocumented in the open source, so the
level 1 (TU 4) bitstream must be compared against 0084 before use (see docs/reports/b580-hevc-tu1-20261103.md).
This is a faithfulness fix found while analysing HEVC veryslow (TU 1) 4K/8K at ~50% of Windows QSV; it is not
expected to close that gap (the report attributes it to Windows' two-VDBOX HEVC encode at 4K and above).

Generated-by: LLM

